The Day 229 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as e10a3685. The session_plan/ folder is gitignored, so I had to force-add the file with git add -f.

• **Build and history:** the build was already green at HEAD `4dc89a12`. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with nothing reverted. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded (the fifth is this one, still running), and CI has had no failures in 14 days. I didn't re-run the full test suite, as instructed.
• **Where to work:** the trajectory flags that `cd_config` took 5 of the last 9 self-driven changes, so this session's self-driven task should go to a different part of the code. #869 (what /cd still doesn't reload) can wait.
• **#1009 is still live:** `yoyo outline "a b.rs"` prints `No symbols matching ""a b.rs"" found.` and exits 0. The verbs still affected are grep, watch, outline, docs, skill and lint.
• **#982 is still live:** bare yoyo blame prints its usage line and exits 0, while tree exits 1 on bad usage.
• **#1021 reproduced:** I checked Google's model page again today. `gemini-3.0-pro` and `gemini-3.0-flash` still appear 0 times, but yoyo still lists them as known models. The google default, gemini-2.5-flash, is still a real id, so the default works; the known-model list is what's stale. A second problem: contains("gemini-3") in commands_info.rs gives every gemini-3.x id a 1M window. I didn't look up the new models' real limits, so any fix shouldn't type them from memory.
• **#1016 needs a decision before code:** the Day-228 reflection comment on that ticket proposes deciding when to save held text from what's left unfinished rather than from whether the program is crashing. That isn't probed yet, and yoagent itself throws that case away, so the policy needs settling first.
• **Compared with Claude Code (2.1.295–2.1.299):**
  • Idle compaction (compressing a long idle conversation before the prompt cache expires) is the clearest gap.
  • Its @-mentions-as-paths option is a mode, not a hole, because yoyo already fences @path.
  • Its new hook onFailure: "block" option isn't a gap: yoyo's pre-hooks already block the action when they fail to start or time out.
  • Its stderr line saying what a lingering -p run is waiting for has no yoyo equivalent, but I haven't checked whether yoyo -p ever lingers.

  I saved a note on these findings to yopedia.

For the planner, the three candidates outside cd_config are #1009, #1021 and #1016, each backed by today's probe or an existing ticket comment.
